From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:09:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] IbashoAgent findPlaces: place search as the directory
 does it, with the account's maturity access

DirPlacesQuery, as LLPanelDirPlaces sends it: words, a parcel category, the most mature rating to include (never
more than the account may enter), sorted by traffic or by name, a page from any start. The replies come back
through a hook in LLPanelDirBrowser::processDirPlacesReply; then each place on the page is asked for as its place
profile asks (ParcelInfoRequest), for its region, position, rating, description and, sorted by name, its traffic.
No quietest-first: Second Life sends the busiest whatever the order asked for.
